# For You

You were not supposed to be reading this.

The material in this archive was recovered after the Shibuya Incident. Much of it was incomplete, damaged, or difficult to verify. Some records contradict others. Some names appear where they should not. Some records appear to have been altered after the fact.

The higher-ups initially dismissed most of this as unreliable.

We are no longer certain.

There is one matter in particular that has remained unresolved.

Suguru Geto was dead.

That fact was established long before the events of Shibuya. And yet, during the incident, witnesses reported seeing him.

The face was his.

The body was his.

The cursed techniques were his.

But those facts alone do not tell us who was standing there.

We have spent enough time looking at names and faces. Neither has given us an answer.

What remains in this archive may.

If you have found this note, then you have already gone further than the people who examined these records before you. Do not discard anything simply because it appears insignificant. A photograph, a date, a name, a missing document—any one of them may explain the rest.

There are pieces of the archive that are no longer here.

Find out why.

— The Higher-Ups
